@q 53:17-23

@qnote 53:21 | The source gives **(a) & (b)**: **phosphorus-32** is the classic treatment for leukaemia and polycythaemia, and **cobalt-60** gamma radiation is used against many cancers.

@table
Radioisotope | Use
**Iodine-131** | **Thyroid** disorders and thyroid cancer
**Cobalt-60** | **Cancer radiotherapy** (gamma rays)
**Phosphorus-32** | **Leukaemia**, blood disorders
**Sodium-24** | **Blood flow** and circulation studies
**Arsenic-74** | Locating **tumours**
Gold-198 | Cancer treatment
Technetium-99m | Most common diagnostic scan isotope
Carbon-14 | Dating ancient material
@end

**Leukaemia** is a cancer with too many **white blood cells**. Modern cancer treatment includes **IMRT** (intensity-modulated radiotherapy), immunotherapy, targeted drugs and India's own **CAR-T cell therapy** (NexCAR19, approved 2023). **Interferons** are antiviral proteins also used against some cancers.

