@q 53:35-42

@table
Eye term | Meaning
**Retina** | Light-sensitive layer where light becomes **nerve impulses**; has the **yellow spot** (sharpest vision) and the **blind spot** (optic nerve exit, no receptors)
**Cataract** | Clouding of the **lens** (none of the listed parts, hence "none of the above")
Glaucoma | Raised pressure inside the eye
**Astigmatism** | Uneven cornea; cylindrical lens
**Myopia** | Sees **near objects clearly**; concave lens
**Hypermetropia** | Image **behind the retina**; convex lens
**Atropine** | Alkaloid (from belladonna) that **dilates the pupil** for eye tests
@end

