@table
Term | Meaning
**MRI** | **Magnetic Resonance Imaging** (magnets and radio waves, no X-rays)
**EEG** | Electroencephalogram: **brain** activity (epilepsy)
ECG / EKG | Heart's electrical activity
EMG | Muscles
**CPR** | **Cardiopulmonary resuscitation**: chest compressions and rescue breaths
**Golden hour** | First hour after a **heart attack** or major injury, when treatment saves most lives
**Cath lab** | Catheterisation lab of **cardiology** (angiography, stents)
**Beta-blockers** | Slow the heart; used after **heart attacks** and for high BP
Bypass graft | Vein from the leg or artery from the chest or forearm, any of these
**Copper-T** | Intra-uterine contraceptive; commonest side effect is **bleeding**
@end

**Aspirin** is an **analgesic** (painkiller) and blood thinner, not an anaesthetic. **Chloromycetin** treats typhoid, **crystal violet** is an antiseptic, and **quinine** fights malaria.

