@section 27.6 | Plant Diseases

@pyq U.P. P.C.S. (Pre) 2022
Match List-I with List-II and select the correct answer from the code given below the lists.
@match
List-I (Plant disease) | List-II (Factor)
A. Citrus Canker | 1. Insect
B. Red rot disease of sugarcane | 2. Deficiency of oxygen
C. Krishnakant disease of potato | 3. Bacteria
D. Sahu disease of wheat | 4. Fungus
@endmatch
Code : A B C D
(a) 1 3 4 2
(b) 1 2 3 4
(c) 4 1 3 2
(d) 3 4 2 1
@ans (*)
@note Citrus canker is **bacterial**, red rot of sugarcane is **fungal** and black heart ("Krishnakant") of potato comes from **lack of oxygen** in storage. The wheat disease meant is **ear cockle** ("Senhu", misprinted "Sahu"), which is caused by a **nematode**, not an insect. Option (d) matches the first three only, so the source marks the question (*).
@end
